From: Chokri Hammedi <52697989+blue0x1@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] graphics: a sparse BDA page table where the GPU can do it

KytyPS5 keeps one GPU address per 16 KB page of the guest's 1.5 TB address
space: a 768 MB device-local buffer, almost all zeros, made at start. On the
PS4 Pro the GPU has about 3.3 GB in all, so that is a quarter of it gone
before a game draws anything; Invincible VS (PPSA30568) runs out of GPU
memory while it loads its menu ("Not enough memory for command submission").

Where the device has sparse residency buffers with non-resident reads that
return zero (RADV on the PS4's GPUs with RADV_EXPERIMENTAL=sparse), the page
table is now a sparse buffer. Memory is bound, zeroed first, only to the 64 KB
pieces of the table that a registered buffer writes to; each covers 128 MB of
guest addresses. KYTY_NO_SPARSE_PAGETABLE=1 keeps the old buffer.

